data.value:
A program or script: .exe, .ps1, .cmd, .bat. You can specify:
**a full path** — C:\Tools\app.exe;
**a path inside the KeyMend scripts folder** — tools\x.ps1; such a rule moves to another computer together with the settings;
**a Windows program name** — notepad.exe.

Programs and scripts are launched with normal permissions, even if KeyMend runs as administrator.

This will:
• copy the program to C:\Program Files\KeyMend\<your name>;
• create a Task Scheduler task that starts this copy with administrator rights when you sign in to Windows, without a UAC prompt;
• turn off normal startup.

Windows will ask for confirmation (UAC). Continue?
